# Build context ignore for `docker build -f investment_ontology_serverpod_server/Dockerfile .`
# (build context is the repo root). Keeps local secrets and dev-only state out
# of the context so they can never be copied into an image layer — the
# Dockerfile's `COPY investment_ontology_serverpod_server ...` would otherwise
# pull config/passwords.yaml and config/admin_emails.local straight into the
# image. Everything else under investment_ontology_serverpod_server/config/,
# web/, migrations/ and assets/ is unaffected and still gets copied.

# Secrets — must never enter the build context.
**/config/passwords.yaml
**/config/admin_emails.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Embedded/local database state and build output — large, irrelevant to the
# compiled server binary, and database content must never enter an image.
# The build stage generates its own .dart_tool/ inside the container via
# `dart pub get`, independent of any host .dart_tool/.
.serverpod/
**/.serverpod/
build/
**/build/
.dart_tool/
**/.dart_tool/

# Version control.
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Editor and agent tooling — not needed to build or run the server.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
.mcp.json
.dart_skills/
skills/
.gstack/
.playwright-mcp/
